        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=3$ or $x=-2$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(x-3)(x+2)&=0\\\\x-3&=0\\quad\\text{or}\\quad x+2=0\\\\x&=3\\quad\\text{or}\\quad x=-2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p15-q5-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "How would you read the solution to the equation $x^2-x-6=0$ from the graph?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Read the x-coordinates where the graph crosses the x-axis: $x=-2$ and $x=3$.",
          "worked": "On the x-axis, $y=0$. Therefore the x-coordinates of the intersections of $y=x^2-x-6$ with the x-axis solve $x^2-x-6=0$: $x=-2$ and $x=3$.",
